===Etymology 2===
From the phrase {{m|en|in the groove}}, originally in reference to the grooves of an early phonograph record.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|dated|slang}} [[cool|Cool]], [[neat]], [[interesting]], [[fashionable]]. {{defdate|popular in the 1940s and again in the 1960s–1970s}}
#* {{quote-book|en|url=https://archive.org/details/hippies00brown/page/20/mode/2up?q=groovy|title=The Hippies|author=Brown, Joe David, ed; Time, inc|publisher=New York, Time|lccn=67030475|oclc=529107|year=1967|text=The hippies do not often try to define the feelings they experience under the influence of psychedelic drugs. Generally they just say, "Oh, '''groovy''', man," or simply, "Wow."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|url=https://archive.org/details/bwb_O6-BAP-463/page/66/mode/2up?q=groovy|title=Groovy Guide to the Guys!|year=1969|text=Basically Bobby’s just a hard-working, highly creative, friendly, '''groovy''' guy who’s got a lot of things he wants to do and is in a hurry to try them all.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Drive By (song lyrics) |author=Pat Monahan (Train) |page= |ISBN= |passage=When you move me, everything is '''groovy'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=May 24, 2012
|author=Nathan Rabin
|title=Film: Reviews: Men In Black 3
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/men-in-black-3,75576/
|page=
|passage=Men In Black 3 lacks the novelty of the first film, and its take on the late ’60s feels an awful lot like a psychedelic dress-up party, all broad caricatures and '''groovy''' vibes.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|actor=Daniel Baxter|title=How It Should Have Ended|season=7|number=3|text=Well, I love it! Move really fast, reverse time, save everyone? That sounds '''groovy'''! I’m gonna have to try that some day!|role=w:Superman|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uT6YOI6JcRs|episode=How X-Men: Days of Future Past Should Have Ended|network=YouTube|publisher=w:How It Should Have Ended|date=Feb 12 2015|writers=Tina Alexander; Daniel Baxter}}

